  "cli_result_text": "Submitted the file set for the Spring Kafka listener container threading refactor across all three repos, ordered by importance:\n\n**spring-kafka (primary implementation)**\n- `AbstractMessageListenerContainer.java` \u2014 base lifecycle/threading contract (SmartLifecycle, phase, error handlers)\n- `KafkaMessageListenerContainer.java` \u2014 single-threaded container being generalized\n- `ConcurrentMessageListenerContainer.java` \u2014 the concurrency wrapper; owns `setConcurrency()`, spawns N `KafkaMessageListenerContainer` children, assigns partitions/executors\n- `MessageListenerContainer.java` \u2014 the container interface (`SmartLifecycle`, `DisposableBean`)\n- `ContainerProperties.java` \u2014 shared config carried into each child container\n- `ConcurrentKafkaListenerContainerFactory.java` / `AbstractKafkaListenerEndpoint.java` / `KafkaListenerEndpoint.java` \u2014 factory/endpoint layer that sets concurrency per `@KafkaListener`\n- `KafkaListenerAnnotationBeanPostProcessor.java` / `EnableKafka.java` \u2014 annotation-driven wiring entry point\n- Test files for both container classes \u2014 needed to update/extend alongside the refactor\n\n**spring-boot (autoconfiguration consumer)**\n- `ConcurrentKafkaListenerContainerFactoryConfigurer.java` \u2014 maps `KafkaProperties.Listener` \u2192 factory/container properties, including `concurrency`\n- `KafkaAutoConfiguration.java` / `KafkaAnnotationDrivenConfiguration.java` \u2014 autoconfig beans wiring the factory\n- `KafkaProperties.java` \u2014 `spring.kafka.listener.concurrency` property surface\n- Integration/unit test files for the autoconfiguration\n\n**spring-framework (core abstractions)**\n- `SmartLifecycle.java` \u2014 lifecycle interface all containers implement\n- `AsyncTaskExecutor.java` / `SimpleAsyncTaskExecutor.java` \u2014 threading primitives `ConcurrentMessageListenerContainer` uses per-child-consumer thread\n\nNote: spring-framework has no Kafka-specific `MessageListenerContainer` (that name only exists for JMS in `spring-jms`); the actual cross-repo dependency is these lower-level `spring-core`/`spring-context` threading and lifecycle abstractions that spring-kafka builds on.",
